# kk: Add a device-local memory type for tiled images
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44929 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
kk: Add a device-local memory type for tiled images

Imported host memory has no MTLHeap, and tiled images need one. Venus
imports guest memory as host pointers on kk, so tiled guest images were
landing there and hitting the assert in kk_image_plane_bind.

This adds a DEVICE_LOCAL-only memory type. Tiled images only use that
one, and host pointer imports only get the host-visible one, so they
can't meet.

Dropped the HOST_TRANSFER filter too: with two types it breaks
identicalMemoryTypeRequirements, and host image copy doesn't map memory
anyway.

CTS memory, api.info, external memory and buffer requirements all pass.
23,040 host_image_copy cases go from Pass to NotSupported because they
ask for host-visible memory on OPTIMAL images.
```
--- src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device_memory.c
+++ src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device_memory.c
@@ -79,8 +79,12 @@ kk_GetMemoryHostPointerPropertiesEXT(
    default:
       return vk_error(dev, VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE);
    }
-   pMemoryHostPointerProperties->memoryTypeBits =
-      BITFIELD_MASK(pdev->mem_type_count);
+   pMemoryHostPointerProperties->memoryTypeBits = 0;
+   for (uint32_t i = 0; i < pdev->mem_type_count; i++) {
+      if (pdev->mem_types[i].propertyFlags &
+          VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT)
+         pMemoryHostPointerProperties->memoryTypeBits |= BITFIELD_BIT(i);
+   }
 
    return VK_SUCCESS;
 }

